Package: nadir
Type: Package
Title: Super Learning with Flexible Formulas
Version: 0.0.1
Authors@R: c( person("Christian", "Testa", , "ctesta@hsph.harvard.edu",
        role = c("aut", "cre"), comment = c(ORCID =
        "0000-0001-9103-5839") ), person("Nima", "Hejazi", , "", role =
        c('ths', 'aut'), comment = c(ORCID = '0000-0002-7127-2789') ))
Description: A functional programming based implementation of the super
        learner algorithm with an emphasis on supporting the use of
        formulas to specify learners. This approach offers several
        improvements compared to past implementations including the
        ability to easily use random-effects specified in formulas
        (like y ~ (age | strata) + ...) and construction of new
        learners is as simple as writing and passing a new function.
        The super learner algorithm was originally described in van der
        Laan et al. (2007)
        <https://biostats.bepress.com/ucbbiostat/paper222/>.
